{"text": "DEPARTMENT OF THE AIR FORCE\nWASHINGTON, DC 20330-1000\n\nOFFICE OF THE SECRETARY\n\n4 Dec 2019\n\nSAF/AAITI (FOIA)\n1000 Air Force Pentagon\nWashington, DC 20330-1000\n\nJames Lawrence\nDept. MR55839\n411A Highland Ave.\nSomerville, MA 02144\n\nDear James Lawrence,\n\nThis is our response to your Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) request, dated 18 June 2019\nfor \"BlindGlint\", \"Blind Glint\", or \"Project BlindGlint\" by name as well as any technologies the\nUnited States Air Force knows of for deleting or modifying commercial aircraft ADS-B\n(Automatic Dependent Surveillance-Broadcast) Data or affecting GNC (Guidance, Navigation,\nand Control) Systems.\u201d\n\nThe Assistant Deputy Chief of Staff/Air, Space & Information Operations (AF/A3) conducted\na reasonable search for responsive records to your request, but none were found. Therefore, a no\nrecords response is provided. The Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) may be able to assist\nyou. Please refer to their website to submit a FOIA request or for their contact information at:\nhttps://www. faa.gov/foia/.\n\nShould you decide that an appeal to this decision is necessary, you must write to the Secretary\nof the Air Force, Thru: SAF/AAII (FOIA), 1000 Air Force Pentagon, Washington, DC 20330-\n1000 within 90 calendar days from the date of this letter. Include in the appeal, your reasons for\nreconsideration, and attach a copy of this letter.\n\nFor any further assistance and to discuss any aspect of your request, please contact the Air\nForce FOIA Public Liaison Officer, Ms. Anh Trinh, at the AF FOIA Public Liaison Office\n(SAF/CN), 1800 Air Force Pentagon, Washington, DC 20330-1800, usaf.pentagon.saf-\ncn.mbx.af-foia@mail.mil or 703-614-8500.\n\nAdditionally, you may contact the Office of Government Information Services (OGIS) at the\nNational Archives and Records Administration to inquire about the FOIA mediation services\nthey offer. The contact information for OGIS is as follows: Office of Government Information\nServices, National Archives and Records Administration, 8601 Adelphi Road-OGIS, College",
